4. CHANNEL -- per row, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs
================================================================================

  row          kills                         observable that differs under it
  ----------   ---------------------------   ------------------------------------------------
  bus ctl      (liveness control)            N/A -- control.  Recorded as N/A, not blank.
  bus ctlsig   (device-signature control)    N/A -- control.
  bus kill     M1_reinstate                  host alive vs dead
  bus attrib   (attribution control)         N/A -- control.
  t1 alive     M1_reinstate                  host alive vs dead
  t1 anchor    M6_busshift, M7_devshift,     the PRINTED TUPLE `bus 1 func 2 device 3'
               M8_busmask, M5_typeswap
  t1 alias     M3_aliasoff, M4_condwrite     PRESENCE of `bus 0 func 0 device 0'
  t1 rdval     M2_nullval                    the synthesised value 0xffff..ffff vs 0
  t0 alive     M9_null                       host alive
  t0 real      M9_null                       a real ID vs empty-slot/unmapped
  t0 accept    M9_null, M5_typeswap          the exact value 0x304848086

*** NO ROW HAS A NON-VARYING CHANNEL.  Every row names a mutant under which its own observable
CHANGES, except the three explicitly marked N/A as controls. ***

*** AND THE CHANNEL LINE EARNED ITS KEEP HERE, BEFORE ANY TABLE RAN -- WHICH IS THE CLAIM THE
CARRIER ASKED THE FIRST MANDATED APPLICATION TO CHECK RATHER THAN OBEY. ***

The carrier says a row's channel-under-its-mutant is knowable at WRITING time.  IT WAS, AND IT
FOUND A FLOOR BREACH BEFORE MEASUREMENT: walking row-by-row for "which mutant makes this differ?"
showed the refusal's own repair expression -- `odata = reg == 0? (uint64_t) -1 : 0' -> `odata = 0'
-- had NO row at all.  It sweeps a 10-row detector clean, because the alias was exercised only by
a WRITE (whose odata is never read) and both control reads take the type-0 path.  `t1 rdval' was
added in response, and my own pass-2 brief had asserted that cell was unobservable.  It is not.

So: the CHANNEL line's claim HELD on its first mandated application, and it caught something the
brief had reasoned wrongly about.  Recorded as a measurement of the rule, not as praise for it.

